WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:05.470
It was an old factory in the middle of nowhere,
long-abandoned but still standing.

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:10.520
In the past, it had been filled with workers,
but now nothing ran through it besides the

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.590
occasional wildlife.

00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.460
One July night in 1949 though, four teenagers
decided it would be a good place to explore.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:24.519
The entrance to the factory was a large, old-fashioned
looking wooden door that was locked tightly

00:00:24.519 --> 00:00:25.519
shut.

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:29.509
The teens looked around for another way in,
but couldn’t find one.

00:00:29.509 --> 00:00:33.780
What they did find though, was an old iron
lockbox.

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:38.650
After some effort, they managed to get the
box open and found a ring of twelve old, rusted

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:41.330
steel keys sitting inside.

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:44.000
Would these old keys open the wooden door?

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.030
Would they find something inside that would
make their night of breaking and entering

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.050
worth it?

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:55.410
If only they knew that by unlocking the door
all they would find was true horror… because

00:00:55.410 --> 00:01:02.970
they had just found SCP-004, better known
as The 12 Keys and the Door

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:08.090
Not long after the local Sheriff received
a call from three of the panicked teens.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:12.210
They explained that while trying to get into
the factory, one of their friends had gone

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.210
missing.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:17.609
The local authorities were quickly deployed,
taking the three teens into custody and beginning

00:01:17.609 --> 00:01:20.140
a full search of the factory grounds.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:24.049
The searching sheriff’s department officers
did eventually manage to find a clue as to

00:01:24.049 --> 00:01:28.829
what happened to the missing teen, but it
wasn’t a good sign.

00:01:28.829 --> 00:01:34.759
It was their severed hand, and even more disturbing
is that it wasn’t discovered outside the

00:01:34.759 --> 00:01:39.889
factory, no, it was found over eight kilometers
away.

00:01:39.889 --> 00:01:45.060
Soon other body parts were also found, some
as far as thirty-two kilometers away, but

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:49.679
how could the parts of the dead teenager’s
body have been scattered so quickly and so

00:01:49.679 --> 00:01:51.310
far from each other?

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:56.909
When the surviving teens were interrogated,
they all repeated the same wild story.

00:01:56.909 --> 00:02:01.670
The now dead teen had taken one of the keys
out of the old box they had found and used

00:02:01.670 --> 00:02:06.659
it to unlock the strange, old-fashioned wooden
door that led into the factory.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:11.819
They opened the door and stepped inside, and
the moment they did, they were immediately

00:02:11.819 --> 00:02:14.730
torn into pieces that suddenly vanished.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:20.450
These were no ordinary keys, and this was
no ordinary door.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:24.209
It was clear this was a job for the SCP Foundation.

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:29.590
An SCP agent was deployed to the site to begin
investigating this anomaly.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:33.950
After getting the keys from local authorities,
the agent brought in a group of twelve D-class

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:37.510
personnel to test them - one for each key.

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:42.319
And it soon became clear that there was one
effect that was common - ten of the keys seemed

00:02:42.319 --> 00:02:46.050
to cause an effect that was completely unsurvivable.

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:50.510
Upon trying the key in the door, the test
subject was immediately torn apart just like

00:02:50.510 --> 00:02:52.500
the unfortunate teenager.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.920
While one key caused the body parts to be
scattered in the immediate vicinity, all the

00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.000
others seemed to vanish into thin air.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:05.400
But it was the other two keys that proved
to be of even greater interest to the Foundation.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:11.730
Unlike with all the other tests, the D-class
using the key designated SCP-004-7 was able

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:14.959
to enter the door and return completely unharmed.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:20.549
But the D-class using SCP-004-12 was a different
story.

00:03:20.549 --> 00:03:26.150
Physically, he returned unharmed - but he
seemed barely able to stagger out of the room.

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:31.150
He collapsed, and then began trying to claw
his eyes out in panic and terror.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:35.659
He was quickly restrained and interrogated,
but he wasn’t coherent enough to give the

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:39.670
Foundation any idea of what lurked behind
the door.

00:03:39.670 --> 00:03:46.469
The first D-class to enter using SCP-004-7,
the one who returned intact and sane, only

00:03:46.469 --> 00:03:51.280
said that it was a massive room inside - far
bigger than the building appeared from the

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.280
outside.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:56.560
It was determined that the use of this key
was safe enough for further testing.

00:03:56.560 --> 00:04:01.220
The door was opened again using the same key
and the Foundation researchers propped it

00:04:01.220 --> 00:04:05.260
open so that an armed team could go in and
hopefully come out.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:10.420
A brief exploration of the massive room showed
some clear anomalous properties - not only

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:16.070
was the room impossible to measure and possibly
limitless in size, it also seemed impossible

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:20.940
to shine any light in the room beyond the
entry and the people inside were the only

00:04:20.940 --> 00:04:24.440
objects that could be felt or illuminated.

00:04:24.440 --> 00:04:28.080
Whatever this room was, it was keeping its
secrets.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:30.650
It was clear the site needed to be locked
down.

00:04:30.650 --> 00:04:34.930
All the initial witnesses who knew too much
were terminated… the Foundation was a little

00:04:34.930 --> 00:04:39.940
more trigger happy with terminations in the
40s, and the site was quickly locked down

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:44.720
under the auspices of it being dangerous due
to unexploded ordinances.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:49.520
Fences were placed around the site so that
there would be no more teenage explorations.

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:53.860
The records are spotty and incomplete, but
whatever happened behind those doors during

00:04:53.860 --> 00:05:00.800
the initial testing between 1949 and 1950,
the Foundation decided it had learned enough.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:06.770
The space-time anomalies at play inside of
SCP-004 were deemed too dangerous to explore

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:11.220
further, and the site was sealed off with
all testing suspended.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:17.090
Whatever was lurking behind those doors, it
would keep its secrets - and the site seemed

00:05:17.090 --> 00:05:19.810
easy to secure and contain.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:26.150
But this was far from the end of SCP-004,
and fifty years later, it made its presence

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.030
known again.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:33.699
It was another July night, many decades after
the unfortunate teenager first opened the

00:05:33.699 --> 00:05:36.610
doors to SCP-004.

00:05:36.610 --> 00:05:41.300
Only a few pieces of their body had been found,
but suddenly, the rest of the corpse appeared

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:46.960
exactly where they had last been seen - outside
the old wooden door.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:51.440
Even odder was the fact that even though the
subject had died many years ago their body

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:56.080
was still fresh, as if they had been killed
that same day.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:59.580
And this wouldn’t be the only sudden reappearance.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:04.289
Two days later, a second body missing parts
appeared in front of the door.

00:06:04.289 --> 00:06:08.650
This was quickly identified as one of the
original twelve test subjects who opened the

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:09.650
door.

00:06:09.650 --> 00:06:13.590
Foundation scientists were once again sent
to the site to explore the space-time anomalies,

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:18.670
and it was becoming clear that what went inside
the door didn’t stay there.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:24.220
It seemed like it went somewhere that didn’t
exist on the same plane as our reality.

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:27.690
And if it could be understood, it could be
used.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:35.670
On March 21st, 1999 the Foundation began establishing
a site inside of SCP-004, but not for testing

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:37.720
or research purposes.

00:06:37.720 --> 00:06:41.970
Nuclear weapons around the world were proliferating
fast, and evidence was mounting that World

00:06:41.970 --> 00:06:44.039
War 3 could happen soon.

00:06:44.039 --> 00:06:48.860
The Foundation needed a site that could survive
anything - and the mysterious room opened

00:06:48.860 --> 00:06:52.890
by the rusted keys seemed like it could be
their salvation.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:57.509
Supplies would go in the room and would be
preserved there indefinitely, safe from even

00:06:57.509 --> 00:06:59.509
nuclear annihilation.

00:06:59.509 --> 00:07:03.289
But getting the site set up would pose its
own challenges.

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:09.129
Now dubbed Site 62, the facility was soon
expanded to house certain SCPs as well, in

00:07:09.129 --> 00:07:13.050
addition to a super-computer to house all
Foundation data.

00:07:13.050 --> 00:07:17.169
This would make it another invaluable backup
in the event of an end-of-the-world event

00:07:17.169 --> 00:07:19.250
that necessitated a reboot.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:23.790
The site was completed over the next year,
during which time they added high-tech containment

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:28.319
units that could hold even the most dangerous
SCP specimens.

00:07:28.319 --> 00:07:32.509
Entering and exiting the facility seemed to
pose a risk to those working on it though.

00:07:32.509 --> 00:07:37.960
Time no longer behaved like it should, even
when using the one safe key.

00:07:37.960 --> 00:07:41.840
People would spend weeks in the site, then
exit claiming they had only been there a few

00:07:41.840 --> 00:07:42.840
days.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:47.389
It was highly unpredictable, and the Foundation
determined that it would be better to eliminate

00:07:47.389 --> 00:07:49.069
this X-factor.

00:07:49.069 --> 00:07:54.380
All personnel working at Site 62 would now
live on-site permanently, with their families

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:57.740
being told they had died in an accident.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:04.380
It was August 18th, 2003 when the United States
and Canada were hit with a massive power outage,

00:08:04.380 --> 00:08:07.889
knocking out power to many of the Northeast’s
biggest population centers.

00:08:07.889 --> 00:08:13.819
While the SCP Foundation has backups on every
site, multiple generators failed, and it was

00:08:13.819 --> 00:08:16.520
53 minutes before power could be restored.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:22.410
During that time, those inside the mysterious
room were plunged into total darkness.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.750
And it soon became clear they weren’t alone.

00:08:26.750 --> 00:08:30.690
In the darkened room, the personnel reported
feeling like they were surrounded by people

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:34.930
that shouldn’t be there - and creatures
that shouldn’t exist.

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:40.010
While they couldn’t see anything and nothing
touched them, they were adamant that something

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:45.620
was lurking in that room, and likely had been
for a very long time.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:50.550
It seemed the limited sources of light may
be the only thing keeping these entities - whatever

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.630
they are - at bay.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:58.180
When testing had resumed on SCP-004 after
the bodies had reappeared outside the door,

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:02.850
the Foundation decided to start exploring
the effects of SCP-004-12 as well.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:08.700
What about this key caused such psychological
horror that subjects would try to tear out

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:10.260
their own eyes?

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:16.310
This key seemed to drive them insane, and
of the sixteen subjects, only four were still

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:19.950
alive for any length of time after their return.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:24.730
Most remained in a catatonic state, but one
was given extensive therapy and regained the

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:29.140
ability to communicate, which allowed him
to give the Foundation their best picture

00:09:29.140 --> 00:09:31.670
yet of what lurked inside the room.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:36.370
While the D-Class personnel was still severely
affected by his time in the room and suffered

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:40.540
near-total amnesia, he did remember a few
things.

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:45.890
He remembered deep terror, and memories being
forced into his mind that made no sense as

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:48.170
if they were artificially implanted.

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:51.410
And he remembered not being alone.

00:09:51.410 --> 00:09:56.660
He described a massive green being, large
enough that he couldn’t see where it began

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.620
and where it ended.

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:00.750
The Foundation didn’t know what it was either.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:05.860
But what they do know for certain is that
when ten of the keys are used, the door is

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:11.899
opened to a dimension where the laws of physics
are so different that it is completely unsurvivable.

00:10:11.899 --> 00:10:16.610
Studies are ongoing as to what makes this
effect so fatal and if there is a way to survive

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:22.060
it, but no answers have been found - and with
only three bodies of victims recovered so

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:25.360
far, there is little evidence

00:10:25.360 --> 00:10:29.660
But one object found on-site is of additional
interest.

00:10:29.660 --> 00:10:33.740
Discovered roughly a year after the initial
anomaly, in a manager’s office on the factory

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:40.110
grounds, SCP-004-14 seems to be a miniature
version of the anomaly.

00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:45.120
It’s a large box made out of wood, and it
is the only other object opened by the one

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:51.490
safe key - as well as five of the other keys
that lead to death when used on the main door.

00:10:51.490 --> 00:10:54.880
And this box has unusual properties as well.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:11:02.370
It opens automatically, and much like SCP-004’s
room, it seems to be much larger on the inside

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:03.760
than the outside.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:06.740
It is possible to come in and out safely.

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:11.330
But when the box is locked again, it’s a
different story.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:15.540
Objects placed in the box don’t seem to
affect its weight, and when the box is closed

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:18.370
and locked, they vanish completely.

00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:23.130
Unlike the main room, nothing that’s gone
inside and locked in has ever been recovered.

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:25.600
This includes living beings.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:30.230
Few answers have been found about where they
go, and it’s possible the box could be used

00:11:30.230 --> 00:11:35.209
to dispose of specimens deemed to be too dangerous
- but with no answers about where they go

00:11:35.209 --> 00:11:39.700
and when they might come back, this may be
too risky.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:45.180
Because SCP-004 is fixed in place, special
containment procedures focus on making sure

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:46.829
it stays that way.

00:11:46.829 --> 00:11:51.280
It is strictly forbidden to take any of the
other keys through the door, for fear of losing

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:54.670
them or causing it to react in an unpredictable
way.

00:11:54.670 --> 00:12:00.490
If the site should be breached, or anything
contained in Site 62 manages escape containment,

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:03.760
the Foundation is ready to activate the on-site
warhead.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.440
Only employees with level 1 clearance can
access the site, and only Level 4s and above

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:13.269
can use the keys - with all knowing that any
attempt to remove the keys from the site will

00:12:13.269 --> 00:12:15.630
result in immediate termination.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:22.370
For now, SCP-004 remains fenced off, with
only select experiments continuing, as the

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.740
Foundation tries to unravel its mysteries.

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:30.930
But whatever lurks behind that old wooden
door, it keeps its secrets well.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:35.900
Now for another location that doesn’t obey
the laws of physics, check out “SCP-354

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:41.740
- The Red Pool”, or watch “SCP-823 - Carnival
of Horrors” for another seemingly normal

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:44.160
location with unexpected dangers.

